# macOS
.DS_Store

# Tier C — project-local, per-member config (design spec addendum §F.7). Templates (*.example)
# ARE committed; the real files are gitignored and never travel with the repo. The env file is
# SHAPEUP_-namespaced (filename + keys) so it never collides with, or gets confused with, the
# target project's own .env / .env.local.
.claude/settings.local.json
.env.shapeup.local
!.env.shapeup.example
!.claude/settings.local.example.json

# ShapeUp SDLC local workspace (ADR-0001 LOCAL tier): per-slug run trace — board, orders/,
# results/, t0/, evaluation/, qa/, orient/, trace/, discovery/, working/, receipt.json — plus
# the checkout-wide active-scope pointer, decisions.jsonl, safety-overrides.json and metrics/.
# The deliverable (shapeup/ — shaping, spec, contracts, requirements, REPORT.md,
# knowledge-base/) stays tracked; only the hidden local root is ignored.
#
# BOTH roots are listed: migration 0006 renames `.shapeup-sdlc/` → `.shapeup/`, and a run trace
# committed during that window is exactly what the tier split exists to prevent.
.shapeup/
.shapeup-sdlc/

# Day-1 / Day-2 measurement instrument, and its run trace.
#
# The split is ADR-0001's, and the line falls between the INSTRUMENT and the RECORDS IT PRODUCES:
#
#   COMMITTED — rubrics (`skills/*/evals/day1-rubric.json`), the committed weak/partial/strong
#     reference drafts, the fixture spine, the row renderers, the three schemas, the Day-2
#     failure-class register, the trigger-eval datasets, and BOTH baselines. This is what a clone
#     needs to re-run the measurement, and `evals/DAY1-REPORT.md` prints
#     `Reproduce: node tools/skill-loop.mjs --measure` on the assumption it is there.
#   IGNORED — `evals/runs/`: raw run records and per-round drafts. 2.3 MB that churns every run,
#     and the machine's business. Structural §48(d7) fails if this line moves in either direction.
#
# Until 2026-08-05 the instrument was ignored too, and the cost was measured rather than argued:
# a clone ran 790 of 1244 structural checks and failed 4, `--selftest` answered `no Day-1 rubrics
# found`, and the report's own Reproduce line was false for every reader but one machine. Keeping
# a paid measurement's apparatus local makes the result unfalsifiable, which is the one thing this
# rung exists to prevent.
#
# `evals/*` rather than `evals/` is load-bearing: git does not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so a `!` negation under `evals/` can never be reached.
evals/*
!evals/baselines/
evals/baselines/*
!evals/baselines/skill-loop.baseline.json
!evals/baselines/trigger-evals.baseline.json
!evals/DAY1-REPORT.md
!evals/README.md
!evals/failure-classes.json
!evals/schemas/
!evals/oracles/
!evals/fixtures/

# The ba-pitch-analyzer reference drafts carry a BOARD, which lives under `.shapeup/` — and the
# run-trace rule at the top of this file matches that name at any depth. Without these two lines
# 66 fixture files drop out of the commit while their fixture directories still look committed,
# and the loop then grades a spec tree with no board against a rubric that expects one. That is
# the HD-001..005 shape exactly: a committed artifact half-read, reported as whole.
!evals/fixtures/**/.shapeup/
!skills/*/evals/fixtures/**/.shapeup/

# Navigator clone target (gap-scan)
example/

# Compiled distribution artifacts (VS Code extension, Antigravity subagents, Cursor rules)
dist/

 # Python cache                                                                                                   
__pycache__/                                                                                                     
*.pyc 


.playwright-mcp

# plan-executor run workspaces (session-independent, never shipped)
.plan-runs/
